From: Balázs Gyimesi <gyimesi.balazs@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: allow disabling SGMII auto-negotiation

0751 enables the QCA8337 SerDes auto-negotiation unconditionally. On the
Xiaomi CB0401V2 the IPQ5018 UNIPHY side of the SGMII link runs forced
(1000/full, no in-band AN, as the stock firmware does): with AN enabled on
the switch the SerDes never syncs and no frame crosses the CPU port.

Add a "qca,sgmii-no-autoneg" CPU port property that keeps AN disabled.

---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1540,9 +1540,11 @@
 {
 	struct qca8k_priv *priv = pcs_to_qca8k_pcs(pcs)->priv;
 	int cpu_port_index, ret, port;
+	struct dsa_port *dp;
 	u32 mask, reg, val;
 
 	port = pcs_to_qca8k_pcs(pcs)->port;
+	dp = dsa_to_port(priv->ds, port);
 	switch (port) {
 	case 0:
 		reg = QCA8K_REG_PORT0_PAD_CTRL;
@@ -1561,8 +1563,13 @@
 
 	/* Enable SerDes auto-negotiation always.
 	 * So fixed-link can work.
+	 * Unless the board runs the other end of the link forced, without
+	 * in-band negotiation (qca,sgmii-no-autoneg): then both ends must be
+	 * forced or the SerDes never syncs.
 	 */
-	ret = qca8k_rmw(priv, QCA8K_REG_PWS, QCA8K_PWS_SERDES_AEN_DIS, 0);
+	val = of_property_read_bool(dp->dn, "qca,sgmii-no-autoneg") ?
+		QCA8K_PWS_SERDES_AEN_DIS : 0;
+	ret = qca8k_rmw(priv, QCA8K_REG_PWS, QCA8K_PWS_SERDES_AEN_DIS, val);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
